W:2. I wish my breast was made of glass
W:Wherein you might behold
W:Oh there your name I's wrote, my dear,
W:In letters made of gold.
W:Oh there your name I's wrote, my dear,
W:Believe me what I say,
W:You are the one I love the best
W:Until my dying day.
W:
W:3. The crow that is so black, my love,
W:will surely turn to white
W:If ever I prove false to you,
W:Bright day return to night.
W:Bright day return to night, my love
W:The elements will mourn,
W:If ever I prove false to you
W:The seas will rage and burn.
W:
W:4. And when you're on some distant shore,
W:Think of your absent friend,
W:And when the wind blows high and clear,
W:A line to me, pray send.
W:And when the wind blows high and clear,
W:Pray send a note to me,
W:That I might know by your handwrite
W:How time has gone with thee.
